# Software Developer (Laravel / Vue.js)
TeamPoint Software
Shrewsbury, United Kingdom / Shrewsbury, England, United Kingdom Salary not disclosed
laravelphpapivue
description
## Job description
Chrome desktop can translate this description on-device without sending the text to LaraBench.
TeamPoint is a UK-developed field service management platform used by service businesses across the country to manage quotations, scheduling, projects, compliance, mobile working, invoicing and business reporting.
For more than 14 years, we have developed and supported our own software, continually improving the platform in partnership with our customers. We are a small, experienced UK team, which means decisions are made quickly, customer feedback directly influences the product and everyone has the opportunity to make a visible contribution.
We are looking for an experienced Software Developer to join TeamPoint in a varied role combining software development with customer support, training and onboarding.
This is not a coding-only position. Alongside designing, developing and improving features using Laravel, Vue.js and MySQL, you will work directly with customers to understand how their businesses operate, help them implement TeamPoint, deliver training and provide ongoing product support.
You will be involved throughout the product lifecycle, from discussing a business requirement and identifying a practical solution through to developing, testing and supporting the finished feature.
### Your responsibilities will include:
* developing new features using PHP, Laravel, Vue.js and MySQL;
* maintaining and improving existing functionality;
* investigating and resolving technical and product-support queries;
* working directly with customers to understand operational requirements;
* supporting customer onboarding and implementation projects;
* delivering online and in-person product training;
* contributing ideas that improve both the software and the customer experience;
* participating in testing, code reviews and technical discussions;
* helping shape the future direction of the TeamPoint platform.
The role is predominantly home based. The successful candidate will need to attend an initial week of training in Shrewsbury and be able to travel to Shrewsbury occasionally afterwards to work with the team. Occasional travel to customer sites, meetings and company events will also be required.
We are looking for someone who enjoys both building good software and working with people.
### You should have commercial experience with:
* PHP;
* Laravel;
* Vue.js;
* MySQL;
* JavaScript;
* Git.
Experience with APIs, automated testing, SaaS platforms, mobile applications or business workflow software would be useful, but is not essential.
### You will also need to:
* communicate clearly and confidently with customers;
* enjoy understanding how different businesses operate;
* explain technical subjects in a practical and accessible way;
* work independently while contributing to a small collaborative team;
* approach problems pragmatically;
* be based in the UK and willing to travel when required.
A degree is not essential. Relevant commercial experience, technical ability and the right approach to customers and teamwork are more important to us.
Our full-time team works four days per week while receiving full-time pay. These are not compressed hours. It is a genuine four-day working week because we believe people produce their best work when they have time to recharge.
You will have the flexibility to work mainly from home while remaining part of a close and collaborative team.
You will see how the software is used in real businesses and have the opportunity to help customers improve the way they work.
Because we are a small team developing our own platform, your ideas and technical contribution will have a visible impact.
The role combines development, support, training and onboarding, giving you a broader understanding of the product and the customers who rely on it.

# Legal Counsel, Structured Finance - Vice President
Apply now »
**Date:** 7 Aug 2026
**Location:**
London (Lon), GB
**Company:** Mizuho
**Profile Summary**
We are seeking an experienced and commercially minded and technically strong lawyer to join our Derivatives and Structured Finance Legal team as a Vice President. The successful candidate will provide legal support to Mizuho’s structured finance business across EMEA, advising on a broad range of structured financing transactions, working closely with front office, structuring, credit, risk and operations teams.
The role will focus principally on structured repo, securities lending, total return swap and other financing transactions, including insurance-wrapped structures, and require familiarity with securitisation and CLO documentation, working with the CIB Structured Financing Group. The successful candidate will act as a trusted legal advisor on complex cross-border financing structures, supporting business growth and effective legal risk management.
This is a business facing role requiring strong technical expertise, commercial judgment and the ability to work collaboratively across multiple business line and jurisdictions and as required, to manage external counsel effectively.
**Duties and Responsibilities**
Provide legal support to Mizuho Bank Ltd., London Branch, Mizuho International plc and Mizuho Bank Europe N.V. and their respective branches and subsidiaries within the EMEA region as follows:
* Provide legal support for a broad range of structured finance and secured financing transactions, including repos, structured repo, securities lending, total return swap and other financing transactions, including insurance-wrapped structures, and require familiarity with securitisation and CLO documentation, synthetic and risk transfer transactions (where applicable) and other structured credit and secured financing products.
* Help structure, negotiate and document complex financing arrangements, balancing commercial objectives with appropriate legal risk management;
* Advise on transaction structuring, legal enforceability, collateral arrangements and insolvency considerations;
* Partner with the business throughout the lifecycle of transactions, from product development and structuring through execution and ongoing management;
* Work closely with external counsel where required and manage legal costs effectively;
* Support strategic business initiatives, new products and platform development;
* Work closely with credit, risk and compliance teams on legal risk management;
* Advise on legal and regulatory developments affecting structured finance and financing markets;
* Contribute to the development of legal templates, internal policies and best practice documentation;
* Provide legal training to the business and infrastructure teams
and:
* Ensure appropriate records are maintained for Legal Services, including the data bases, directories and documentation management necessary to record transactions / matters worked on; and
* Support their manager to ensure know-how, policies, procedures and playbooks are maintained and reviewed at least annually and in response to any material developments.
**Qualifications, Skills, and Experience**
* Qualified solicitor of at least 5-9 years’ PQE, with structured finance experience gained through an international bank, a law firm with a structured finance practice or a combination of the two;
* Strong understanding of structured financing products and transaction execution and preferably with cross-border experience;
* Strong knowledge of structured finance and securitisation principles, security interests and collateral arrangements, insolvency and creditor rights, financial markets regulation affecting structured finance.
* Experience in one or more of the following products would be desirable or advantageous: structured derivatives, structured repos and GMRA documentation, CLO establishment and ongoing management, securitisation programmes (public and private), insurance wrapped financing structures, asset backed lending, fund finance and managed account platforms, regulatory capital transactions or private credit financing structures.
* Strong client service orientation;
* Great organisational and time management skills, with ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines;
* Excellent communication, negotiation and stakeholder management skills;
* Demonstrable ability to innovate, support change and problem solve;
* Demonstrable commercial judgment, balancing commercial objectives and legal risk;
* Ability to work independently, while recognising where escalation is appropriate;
* High attention to detail;
* Cultural awareness and ability to work effectively with colleagues across different jurisdictions; and
* Collaborative nature to contribute to a successful team and departmental performance, fostering the spirit of teamwork and cohesiveness.
**What Mizuho can offer you**
Here at Mizuho, there are fantastic progression opportunities and clear paths to promotion. We will give you ample opportunity to affect change and to help grow our business.
In addition to the great opportunity outlined above we are also currently able to offer:
* Competitive starting salary, plus discretionary bonus
* Non-contributory pension
* 27 days’ annual leave
* Core working hours\*
* Hybrid working - office and home based\*
* Virtual GP
* Wellbeing benefits, including Mental Health Allies and First Aiders
\**For applicable roles only*
**At Mizuho, we embrace flexible ways of working when the role permits. We offer different working arrangements like part-time, job-sharing and hybrid (office and home) working. Our purpose-led culture and global infrastructure help us connect, collaborate, and work together in agile ways to meet all our business needs.**
**At Mizuho we are committed to supporting equality, diversity and equality, and seek to create a workplace that is fully inclusive. We welcome applications from all sections of the community that we operate in and from all ethnic backgrounds, sexual orientation, beliefs, gender identities and disabilities.**
**If you require more information about our equal opportunities policy or wish to discuss any accessibility requirements or reasonable adjustments please contact the recruitment team – recruitment@mizuhoemea.com and we will be happy to help.**
Apply now »

# Underwriting Oversight Assistant
**Standort** London, Vereinigtes Königreich
**Art der Arbeit** Vollzeit
**Arbeitsform** Hybrid
**Job level** Berufserfahrene
**Job ID** 13720
**Unternehmen** Munich Re Specialty - Global Markets
**Anstellungsart** Unbefristet
**Fachbereich** Schadenbearbeitung und Underwriting
Jetzt bewerben
About us
At Munich Re Specialty – Global Markets (MRS-GM), it is our ambition to become the leading Primary Specialty Insurance provider, underpinned by an effective and adaptable strategy, superior products and industry leaders working in a supportive environment to achieve this.
At the heart of our success is a strong culture where people are encouraged to be present, bold and curious, allowing them to achieve their individual goals.
Please see our website for more information.
Underwriting Oversight Assistant
We are currently looking for a Underwriting Oversight Assistant to be based in London on a full-time basis, reporting into the Group Head of Underwriting Oversight.
In this role, you will support underwriting activities within Munich Re Specialty – Global Markets. You will play a key part in maintaining the monitoring structure, oversight, and operational processes necessary to meet underwriting standards in accordance with Munich Re Group guidelines and the Lloyd’s Principles Based Oversight framework. Success in this position requires strong communication skills, an analytical mindset, and a genuine eagerness to deepen your knowledge and develop your analytical abilities.
This role is open to school leavers and recent graduates.
Responsibilities:
* Conduct regular performance monitoring of peer reviews and 4-eyes reviews, following up with underwriters to ensure findings are appropriately actioned;
* Support analysts with regular sample reviews of LIC risks to ensure adherence to the LIC operating model, including recording and tracking any necessary actions;
* Assist with tracking policy and portfolio performance and support the Portfolio Management team;
* Support the production of regular Underwriting Oversight reports for MRSL committees and provide underwriting reports and data extracts as required by internal stakeholders;
* Assist with data collection and file administration for key review functions such as Independent Peer Review, Central Underwriting reviews, and internal audits;
* Provide administrative support in maintaining the team SharePoint site, wider intranet, and monitor the team mailbox including maintaining logs of underwriter referrals and dispensations;
* Support scheduling and minute taking for internal meetings;
* Provide support to underwriters in navigating and staying up to date with the latest Munich Group and local underwriting policies and guidelines;
* Attend regular team and underwriter meetings to maintain current knowledge and understanding of relevant topics and assist with ad-hoc tasks from other areas of the business as needed;
* Help drive forward good conduct within the business to deliver the best outcomes for customers and policyholders.
Knowledge and Skills Essential:
* Keen interest in the Lloyd’s insurance market;
* Analytical mindset;
* Good organisation skills;
* Strong communication skills;
* Willingness to develop knowledge of insurance disciplines including Underwriting, Pricing and Claims.
Preferred:
* Basic awareness of FCA / PRA regulations;
* Basic awareness of the Lloyd’s Principles for doing business and oversight framework;
* Basic knowledge and understanding of the underlying principles of insurance and reinsurance.
If you are excited about this role but your experience does not align perfectly with everything outlined, or you don’t meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply anyway. You might just be the candidate we are looking for!
Diversity, Equity & Inclusion
At Munich Re, Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion foster innovation and resilience and enable us to act braver and better. Embracing the power of DEI is at the core of who we are. We recognise diversity can be multi-dimensional, intersectional, and complex, so we want to build a diverse workforce that includes a wide range of racial, ethnic, sexual, and gender identities; economic and geographic backgrounds; physical abilities; ages; life, school, and career experiences; and political, religious, and personal beliefs. Additionally, we are committed to building an equitable and inclusive work environment where this diversity is celebrated, valued, and has equitable opportunities to succeed.
All candidates in consideration for any role can request a reasonable adjustment at any point in our recruitment process. You can request an adjustment by speaking to your Talent Acquisition contact.
Learning and innovating today, striving for sustainable societies and business tomorrow
At Munich Re Specialty – Global Markets our approach to ESG is underpinned by our desire to seize business opportunities and to nurture a stimulating and inclusive work environment. Our ESG strategy aims to deliver holistic impacts across environmental, social and governance topics including supporting a number of local initiatives within our community and offering volunteering opportunities for colleagues.
Learn more about sustainability at Munich Re (wird in einem neuen Fenster geöffnet) – choose your impact!
