## Parts Sales Manager
Due to the continued growth in our business, we are now seeking to recruit a highly organised and strategic Parts Sales Manager to drive growth across our dealer network.
The role of Parts Sales Manager will play a pivotal role in providing first class delivery, service and support in developing a growing spare parts business to our global dealer network. This role will plan, organise and direct all parts sales, pulling together all elements of sourcing, procurement and sales to ensure a seamless pathway from order to dispatch. The role interfaces with and acts as the link between all functions including the Sales and Engineering teams, external suppliers, order processing, shipping and our dealer networks.
This is an exciting opportunity for someone with experience in parts sales, aftermarket and dealer development who is commercially focused, enjoys building relationships, identifying sales opportunities and using data to improve underlying business performance.
Working across both office and field activities, you will collaborate with our ever-expanding network of dealers and all facets of our internal teams to increase parts sales, enhance customer satisfaction and support the continued growth of our aftermarket business.
## Key Aspects of the Role
* Develop and grow spare parts sales across an established dealer network;
* Support our dealer network with inventory planning, parts availability and sales growth opportunities;
* Work with our dealer network to improve parts availability, inventory planning, quotation-to-order conversion and customer satisfaction;
* Analyse sales performance, market trends and customer data to identify growth opportunities;
* Develop reporting tools to improve dealer performance;
* Build strong and lasting relationships with all dealers and internal stakeholders;
* Provide regular business updates, sales reports and market intelligence to the Leadership team; and
* Support new product launches, sales campaigns and dealer training initiatives.
## Your Experience & Skillset
* Degree Educated and/or equivalent experience in parts sales, inventory planning, dealer network development, product support, and aftermarkets service;
* Strong Commercial awareness with the ability to convert opportunity into order;
* Demonstratable leadership and interpersonal skills including the ability to interact effectively and professionally with individuals at all levels – both internally and externally;
* Proven track record in managing and growing a team;
* Proven ability to work in a fast-paced environment and manage multiple priorities across both the office and field environments;
* Strong communication (written and spoken), negotiation, problem-solving and follow-up skills;
* Fluency in working with all aspects of MS Office suite, CRM software and financial reporting platforms;
* Excellent presentation and interpersonal skills;
* Self- motivated, well-organised and excels at cultivating a true team spirit;
* An element of travel will be required.
The above job description is non-exhaustive and there may be additional duties in accordance with the role.
